figdown 0.1 block
# The COMPANION to 950, and the limit of core §13.4's promise. This document
# is the same six-release chain, plus one construct that was WITHDRAWN rather
# than renamed (`layer`, whose target `plane` went, `PAINT-ORDER-CONSTRUCT`).
# §13.4 promises mechanical migration for FROZEN constructs; `plane` was
# EXPERIMENTAL, so none was owed. The chain therefore HALTS: the withdrawn
# lines are reported and left alone, which strands `node a` — an erroring line
# declares no id — so the rewritten `pin a` line is a NEW error and refusal (c)
# refuses the whole file rather than write it. A human deletes the two lines
# and re-runs; that is the cost `PAINT-ORDER-CONSTRUCT` accepted, priced here rather than assumed.
layer over "Overlay"
node a "A" layer=over
node b "B" shape=diamond
node c "C"
external e "Upstream"
edge a -> b
edge a -> e
layout
pin a at=(20,20)
pin b width=100 height=40
